---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import {
  CollapsibleHero,
  CollapsibleTriggers,
  CollapsibleMotion,
  CollapsibleChat,
  CollapsibleReviewCard,
  CollapsibleSidebar,
  CollapsibleStates,
} from '../../components/CollapsibleDemo';
---

<Docs title="Collapsible" description="Show and hide one region of details, lists, or settings in place.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Collapsible</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A trigger that shows and hides one region in place. Use it for details, longer lists, and settings that most people
    do not need every time.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="collapsible-demo">
    <CollapsibleHero client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Collapsible usage"
      code={`import {
  Collapsible,
  CollapsibleContent,
  CollapsibleTrigger,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/collapsible";
import { Button } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/button";

<Collapsible>
  <CollapsibleTrigger render={<Button variant="ghost" size="sm" />}>
    Approval details
  </CollapsibleTrigger>
  <CollapsibleContent>
    <p>Only the listed changes are approved.</p>
  </CollapsibleContent>
</Collapsible>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>Collapsible</code> holds the open state. Pass <code>defaultOpen</code> to let it manage itself, or{' '}
      <code>open</code> and <code>onOpenChange</code> to control it. <code>disabled</code> blocks the trigger.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Triggers</h2>
    <p>
      The trigger is unstyled. Give it a Sprõut <code>Button</code> with <code>render</code>. Use <code>outline</code>{' '}
      for a main section, <code>ghost</code> for secondary details, <code>xs</code> and <code>link</code> inside dense
      status rows, and
      <code>chat-row</code> for full-width rows inside a list.
    </p>
    <CollapsibleTriggers client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Content variants</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Content variants"
      code={`<CollapsibleContent>…</CollapsibleContent>               // instant
<CollapsibleContent variant="sidebar">…</CollapsibleContent> // height and fade
<CollapsibleContent variant="card">…</CollapsibleContent>    // height only`}
    />
    <CollapsibleMotion client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Indicators</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Turning chevrons"
      code={`<CollapsibleTrigger>
  <Sparkle aria-hidden="true" />
  Thought for 12s
  <ChevronDown aria-hidden="true" data-slot="collapsible-indicator" />
</CollapsibleTrigger>

<ChevronRight
  aria-hidden="true"
  data-slot="collapsible-indicator"
  data-direction="right"
/>`}
    />
    <p>
      Mark a chevron with <code>data-slot="collapsible-indicator"</code> and it turns 180° while open. Add{' '}
      <code>data-direction="right"</code> for a right chevron that turns 90°. It works inside the trigger, and anywhere
      in the header outside the content, so a chevron can sit beside a badge. To swap the icon or label instead, read
      the state you control.
    </p>
    <CollapsibleChat client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Cards</h2>
    <p>
      Put the trigger in the heading and stretch its hit area over the header with a pseudo-element. Control{' '}
      <code>open</code> to close the card when the review settles.
    </p>
    <CollapsibleReviewCard client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Sidebar</h2>
    <p>
      Render a <code>SidebarMenuAction</code> as the trigger and use the <code>sidebar</code> content variant. Close the
      list while the sidebar shows only icons.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Sidebar recent items"
      code={`const { isMobile, state } = useSidebar();
const visible = open && (isMobile || state === "expanded");

<Collapsible open={visible} onOpenChange={setOpen}>
  <SidebarMenuButton …>Chats</SidebarMenuButton>
  <CollapsibleTrigger
    aria-label={\`\${visible ? "Collapse" : "Expand"} Chats\`}
    render={<SidebarMenuAction />}
  >
    <ChevronRight data-slot="collapsible-indicator" data-direction="right" />
  </CollapsibleTrigger>
  <CollapsibleContent variant="sidebar">
    <SidebarMenuSub aria-label="Recent chats">…</SidebarMenuSub>
  </CollapsibleContent>
</Collapsible>`}
    />
    <CollapsibleSidebar client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">States</h2>
    <p>
      Content can sit before the trigger so a list grows from its button. <code>keepMounted</code> keeps closed content
      in the page, so form state and scroll position survive. Pass <code>open</code> with no trigger to show a fixed
      list.
    </p>
    <CollapsibleStates client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="collapsible-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <p>
      The three parts wrap Base UI Collapsible. Every Base UI prop works, including <code>render</code>,{' '}
      <code>keepMounted</code>, <code>hiddenUntilFound</code>, and <code>className</code> as a string or a state
      function.
    </p>
    <p>
      Parts get <code>data-slot</code> values of <code>collapsible</code>, <code>collapsible-trigger</code>, and{' '}
      <code>collapsible-content</code>. Pass your own <code>data-slot</code> to rename a root. The root has{' '}
      <code>data-open</code> or <code>data-closed</code>, the trigger has <code>data-panel-open</code>, and the content
      has <code>data-variant</code> plus Base UI's starting and ending style attributes.{' '}
      <code>collapsibleContentVariantNames</code> lists the variants.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The trigger is a button with <code>aria-expanded</code> and <code>aria-controls</code>. Enter and Space toggle it.
      Give icon-only triggers an <code>aria-label</code> that names the action, and link a disabled trigger to its
      reason with <code>aria-describedby</code>. Put the trigger inside a heading when it names a section.
    </p>
    <p>Chevrons turn over 120ms and animated content grows over 180ms. Both stop when reduced motion is requested.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Collapsible uses <code>--sprout-focus</code>, <code>--sprout-radius-control</code>,{' '}
      <code>--sprout-motion-fast</code>, <code>--sprout-motion-normal</code>, and <code>--sprout-motion-ease</code>.
      Everything else comes from the trigger and content you render, so it follows light, dark, and the TulipFarm theme.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
